{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CfrviuRJ9j8BzKWgUvA6C","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The `fetcher` package is now asyncio-based, and the suite passes: 6 tests, run with `python3 -m pytest -q` on Python 3.14.\n\nWhat changed:\n\n- **`fetcher/client.py`**: `get`, `get_many`, and `close` are async, and `async with` is supported. The transport is an async callable, and the default transport uses `asyncio.sleep(0.01)`. Retries keep the same policy (`retries` attempts, exponential backoff via `asyncio.sleep`, retry only on `TransientError`). `get_many` runs requests under an `asyncio.Semaphore(max_concurrency)`, with `max_concurrency=5` as the default. It uses `gather`, so results keep input order, and per-URL exceptions come back as `FetchError` entries.\n- **`fetcher/aggregate.py`**: `summarize` is async and returns the same dict shape.\n- **`fetcher/sync.py`** (new): `fetch_all(urls, transport=None)` runs the async client under `asyncio.run` and returns the `get_many` result list.\n- **`tests/test_client.py`**: ported to plain `asyncio.run`, so no new dependency. I added two tests: one checking that concurrency is capped at `max_concurrency` and that order is preserved, and one covering the sync wrapper with a custom transport.\n\nChoices I made:\n- I used `asyncio.run` in the tests rather than pytest-asyncio, to avoid adding a dependency.\n- The semaphore is created per `get_many` call, not in `__init__`, so a `Client` can be built outside a running loop.\n\nI did not commit anything, since you didn't ask for a commit."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2661,"cache_read_input_tokens":44134,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2661},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"02e1da28-84a2-4ed8-ae81-edac7ff176a1","uuid":"8d166a39-14f7-4ceb-9f81-ad2cc61b24dc","timestamp":"2026-10-09T15:49:05.168Z","request_id":"req_011Cfrviu1VHnaUV4ZXu2hAg"}
